[Music]  the falcon in the winter soldier is full  of everything that makes the mcu special  including a ton of easter eggs from  references to past movies to homages to  the comic books that inspired the mcu  the disney plus show is bursting with  small details  here are some you might have missed the  falcon in the winter soldier opens with  a stunning action set piece featuring  the falcon performing a daring rescue  if the leader of the airborne kidnappers  looks familiar to you there's a very  good reason  that's none other than georges batroc  the dangerous mercenary who steve rogers  fights in the opening scenes of captain  america the winter soldier  he is played in both the film and the  falcon in the winter soldier by mma  legend george st  pierre in winter soldier captain america  runs up against batroc while rescuing  hostages aboard a shield ship which  batroc is hijacked  of course comic readers know batrock  better as batroc the leaper  a goofy kickboxing master has been a  thorn in captain america's side since  his debut in 1966's tales of suspense  number 75  putting sam wilson up against a classic  captain america baddie thus showing that  the falcon is just as capable of steve  rogers when it comes to taking on  supervillain threats is a candy way for  the falcon and the winter soldier to set  the stage early  you may not believe it yet but sam  wilson is absolutely steve's equal  just ask batrock in the falcon and the  winter soldier bucky barnes isn't sam  wilson's only partner in crime fighting  the falcon also teams up with a young  american gi named joaquin torres  in the first episode of the series  torres provides sam with operational  support while he's tussling with  batroc's forces  he later infiltrates a flag smash rally  in order to figure out what the  terrorist organization is up to  joaquin's connection to the falcon goes  much deeper than mere friendship though  torres made his comics debut in 2015's  captain america sam wilson  he emerges during a period in which sam  wilson has taken over steve rogers's  superhero identity  as a mexican-american living in arizona  torres is concerned about the well-being  of the immigrant community  unfortunately joaquin's good intentions  attract the attention of the sons of the  serpent  a racist terrorist group that capture  him and ship him off to dr carl malus  for experimentation  malice uses the dna from wilson's actual  falcon red wing to mutate torres giving  him wings and the same psychic link with  red wing that wilson enjoys  eventually wilson rescues torres but the  mutations are permanent  thus torres takes on the mantle of the  falcon and becomes the new captain  america's faithful sidekick  some people some people they think that  he's  in a secret base on the moon looking  down  over us the conspiracy theory torres  shares about steve rogers is not as  silly as it sounds  in marvel comics all sorts of characters  live on the moon most notably the moon  is home to the inhumans a genetically  enhanced offshoot of human race  technically the inhumans are already  part of the mcu they're the subject of  2017's short-lived inhuman series which  received four reviews and was cancelled  very quickly  uatu the watcher a mysterious alien  being who observes human history but is  forbidden from interfering  also lives on earth's biggest satellite  most likely however taurus line is a sly  reference to none other than nick fury  in the comics fury spends a few years on  the moon where he takes over owatu's  responsibilities  in the lionwide crossover known as  original sin fury kills owatu and steals  one of his eyes in order to solve an  outer space mystery  as punishment the rest of the watchers  imprison fury on the moon dub him the  unseen and force him to watch over earth  helpless to assist as further  catastrophes unfold  thankfully for fury his punishment  doesn't last oawatu eventually returns  from the dead and relieves fury of his  duties  steve rogers isn't in the falcon in the  winter soldier but his legacy looms  large over the entire series  after donating steve's shield to the  smithsonian institution sam wilson and  james rhodes aka war machine  take a walk through the museum's captain  america exhibit the fictional exhibit is  dominated by steve's world war ii  exploits the motorcycle on the prop  shield he used during uso shows as seen  in captain america the first avenger  figure prominently look a little closer  and you'll also see a picture of the 4f  classification that originally kept  steve rogers from enlisting  among other doodads and mementos the  most important artifact however is  captain america comics number one  this item is much bigger than the mcu of  course and exists in our world as well  this 1941 comic written by joe simon and  drawn by jack kirby contains captain  america and bucky's debut  its cover which depicts cap punching  hitler in the jaw was considered  particularly bold at the time  the comic came out a year before america  officially entered the war and its  overtly political message inspired so  much public anger simon and kirby were  assigned police protection  the first episode of the series  introduces a new threat to the mcu  the flag smashers the flag smashers are  a group of terrorists who fight for a  world without borders and believe that  life in the mcu is better during the  blip  as you probably guessed the  flagsmasher's origin comes from the  comics  although the original flagsmasher is a  single man not an organization  carl morgenthau is a skilled martial  artist who dreams of being a diplomat  when carl's father is killed however the  young activist decides that violence is  the only way to achieve peace  he thus adopts the moniker flag smasher  and begins a one-man terror operation  so far that's pretty different from the  falcon and the winter soldiers take on  the flag smashers  but don't think it isn't related aaron  kellyman appears in the first episode's  end credits as carly morgenthau a  gender-swapped version of carl  if you look closely you can tell she's  the flag smasher handing out mass during  the bank robbery in switzerland  if you pause the episode when bucky  pulls out his little notebook you'll see  a couple of names familiar to fans of  marvel comics and one established mcu  villain  helmut zemo is a sokovian terrorist who  first appeared in captain america civil  war  he framed the winter soldier for the  death of black panther's father which  kicked off the film's namesake civil war  between the avengers  other notable names on the list include  aerostar most likely andre rustoff aka  the red barbarian an old iron man  villain there's also w  hausa a possible reference to captain  willem hausa a nazi soldier who appeared  in a nick fury comic in 1966.  prolific marvel comics writer len  kaminsky co-creator of war machine's  armor also gets a shout out  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the falcon and the winter soldier coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you

